href="hejohns.xml"
addr="hejohns"
title="Johnson He">Johnson He</fr:link></fr:author></fr:authors><fr:parent>hejohns-000E</fr:parent></fr:frontmatter><fr:mainmatter><fr:p>
        An adjunction core extends to an adjuction iff <fr:tex
display="inline"><![CDATA[∀a,b ∈ A. ∀x ∈ X.]]></fr:tex>
        <fr:link
type="local"
href="subb-000E.xml"
addr="subb-000E"
title="Untitled › I">I</fr:link> commutes, and iff <fr:tex
display="inline"><![CDATA[∀x,y ∈ X. a ∈ A.]]></fr:tex> <fr:link
type="local"
href="subbb-000E.xml"
addr="subbb-000E"
title="Untitled › II">II</fr:link>
        commutes.
        The adjunction is unique when it exists.
    </fr:p><fr:p>
        The <fr:link
type="local"
href="street-2012.xml"
addr="street-2012"
title="The Core of Adjoint Functors">original theorem</fr:link> is stated in terms of
        <fr:tex
display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {V}]]></fr:tex>-enriched categories, but we only treat the simple case
        of Homset-categories here.
    </fr:p><fr:tree
